  "Scripture is Louis Segond 1910 (fra_lsg), pasted by script where Wigglesworth quotes the KJV. Where Segond shifts his point the verse is kept and flagged: Luc 12:50 (combien il me tarde vs. straitened), Joël 3:21 (vengerai vs. cleanse), Actes 26:18 (par la foi goes with forgiveness), Rom 14:9 (dominer vs. be Lord of); 1 Jean 4:4 is adapted to his “in me”.",
  "AI-translated (job #6254) in parallel chapters, then reconciled for one form per term (pentecôtiste, baptême du Saint-Esprit, dons de l’Esprit, païens). English slips noted, not fixed: “1 had received” (I had), Acts 4:30 cited for 4:31, and typos such as abunance, delivance, understook, Scandanavia, minstry. Awaiting native review."
